{"page":{"id":"da9879fd-fc66-43a9-b4b9-19993e1d7a92","theme":"dungeons-and-dragons","slug":"/dungeons-and-dragons","canonical_url":"https://www.tonolore.com/dungeons-and-dragons","title":"Dungeons & Dragons","meta_title":"Dungeons & Dragons (Dungeons & Dragons) — topic, lore & connections | Ton-o-Lore","meta_description":"Dungeons & Dragons is the tabletop role-playing game published by Wizards of the Coast, spanning editions from Gary Gygax and Dave Arneson's original rules…","content":"<section class=\"intro\">\n    <p class=\"lead\">\n        <a href=\"/dungeons-and-dragons/hasbro/wizards-of-the-coast\" class=\"entity-link\">Wizards of the Coast</a>&#039;s tabletop fantasy RPG of dice, classes, and shared worlds.\n    </p>\n\n    \n    <p>\n        Key threads from this canonical page lead to\n        <a href=\"/dungeons-and-dragons/gary-gygax\" class=\"entity-link\"><strong>Gary Gygax</strong></a>, <a href=\"/dungeons-and-dragons/dnd-fifth-edition\" class=\"entity-link\"><strong>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</strong></a>, <a href=\"/dungeons-and-dragons/hasbro/wizards-of-the-coast\" class=\"entity-link\"><strong>Wizards of the Coast</strong></a>, <a href=\"/dungeons-and-dragons/dave-arneson\" class=\"entity-link\"><strong>Dave Arneson</strong></a>, <a href=\"/dungeons-and-dragons/dungeon-master\" class=\"entity-link\"><strong>Dungeon Master</strong></a> and <a href=\"/dungeons-and-dragons/original-dungeons-dragons\" class=\"entity-link\"><strong>Original Dungeons &amp; Dragons (1974)</strong></a>.\n        Each link is another long-tail path through the subject.\n    </p>\n\n</section>\n\n\n\n\n\n<section class=\"connection-narrative\">\n    <h2>How Dungeons &amp; Dragons connects</h2>\n    <p>\n        These mapped links are unique to this page — each one is another\n        long-tail route through the subject graph.\n    </p>\n    <ul>\n        \n        <li>\n            <strong>Created By:</strong>\n            <a href=\"/dungeons-and-dragons/gary-gygax\" class=\"entity-link\">Gary Gygax</a>\n            — <a href=\"/dungeons-and-dragons/gary-gygax\" class=\"entity-link\">Gary Gygax</a> co-created Dungeons &amp; Dragons.\n        </li>\n        <li>\n            <strong>Contains:</strong>\n            <a href=\"/dungeons-and-dragons/dnd-fifth-edition\" class=\"entity-link\">Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</a>\n            — 5e is the current D&amp;D edition.\n        </li>\n        <li>\n            <strong>Published By:</strong>\n            <a href=\"/dungeons-and-dragons/hasbro/wizards-of-the-coast\" class=\"entity-link\">Wizards of the Coast</a>\n            — <a href=\"/dungeons-and-dragons/hasbro/wizards-of-the-coast\" class=\"entity-link\">Wizards of the Coast</a> publishes D&amp;D.\n        </li>\n        <li>\n            <strong>Created By:</strong>\n            <a href=\"/dungeons-and-dragons/dave-arneson\" class=\"entity-link\">Dave Arneson</a>\n            — <a href=\"/dungeons-and-dragons/dave-arneson\" class=\"entity-link\">Dave Arneson</a> co-created Dungeons &amp; Dragons.\n        </li>\n        <li>\n            <strong>Contains:</strong>\n            <a href=\"/dungeons-and-dragons/dungeon-master\" class=\"entity-link\">Dungeon Master</a>\n            — The DM runs D&amp;D sessions.\n        </li>\n        <li>\n            <strong>Contains:</strong>\n            <a href=\"/dungeons-and-dragons/original-dungeons-dragons\" class=\"entity-link\">Original Dungeons &amp; Dragons (1974)</a>\n            — The 1974 rules began the D&amp;D line.\n        </li>\n        <li>\n            <strong>Contains:</strong>\n            <a href=\"/dungeons-and-dragons/forgotten-realms\" class=\"entity-link\">Forgotten Realms</a>\n            — The Realms are D&amp;D&#039;s flagship setting.\n        </li>\n        <li>\n            <strong>Contains:</strong>\n            <a href=\"/dungeons-and-dragons/advanced-dungeons-dragons\" class=\"entity-link\">Advanced Dungeons &amp; Dragons</a>\n            — AD&amp;D is a major historical edition.\n        </li>\n    </ul>\n</section>\n\n\n<section class=\"graph-section\">\n    <h2>Mapped connections</h2>\n\n    <p class=\"section-intro\">\n        Every edge is another route through the subject. Expand a group\n        to see how these threads fit together.\n    </p>\n\n    \n<section class=\"topic-section\">\n    <details>\n        <summary class=\"topic-summary\">\n            <span class=\"topic-title\">Contains</span>\n            <span class=\"topic-count\">10</span>\n        </summary>\n\n        \n        <div class=\"topic-examples\">\n            \n                <a\n                    href=\"/dungeons-and-dragons/dnd-fifth-edition\"\n                    class=\"connection\"\n                    data-relationship=\"Contains\"\n                >\n                    <strong>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</strong>\n                    <span>Current streamlined edition of D&amp;D.</span>\n                </a>\n            \n                <a\n                    href=\"/dungeons-and-dragons/dungeon-master\"\n                    class=\"connection\"\n                    data-relationship=\"Contains\"\n                >\n                    <strong>Dungeon Master</strong>\n                    <span>Referee who runs a D&amp;D game.</span>\n                </a>\n            \n                <a\n                    href=\"/dungeons-and-dragons/original-dungeons-dragons\"\n                    class=\"connection\"\n                    data-relationship=\"Contains\"\n                >\n                    <strong>Original Dungeons &amp; Dragons (1974)</strong>\n                    <span>The first published D&amp;D rules set.</span>\n                </a>\n            \n        </div>\n        \n\n        <div class=\"topic-content\">\n            \n                <div class=\"fact-card\">\n                    <div class=\"fact-label\">\n                        Contains\n                    </div>\n\n                    